---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---
<Layout
  title="privacy"
  description="How the adore Discord bot collects, uses, and protects your data."
>
  <Prose heading="privacy policy" updated="June 2026">
    <p>
      This policy explains what data <strong>{site.name}</strong> collects and how
      it is used. We collect only what is needed to provide the bot's features.
    </p>

    <h2>what we store</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Server and channel IDs, and configuration you set (prefix, colors, settings).</li>
      <li>User IDs for features you use (economy balances, levels, reminders, warnings).</li>
      <li>Message content only when required by a command you run (e.g. embeds, snipe), and only as long as needed.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>what we do not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We do not sell your data.</li>
      <li>We do not log or read messages outside of commands you explicitly invoke.</li>
      <li>We do not share data with third parties except integrations you opt into (e.g. Spotify, Last.fm).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Optional integrations (Spotify, Last.fm, AI providers) process data
      according to their own privacy policies when you connect or use them.
    </p>

    <h2>data removal</h2>
    <p>
      You can request deletion of your data, or your server's data, by contacting
      us in the
      <a href={site.support} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">support server</a>.
      Removing the bot stops further data collection for your server.
    </p>

    <h2>changes</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy. Material changes will be announced in the support server.</p>
  </Prose>
</Layout>
